#: results.md:1
msgid "[&larr; Home](NAVIGATION.md)"
msgstr "[&larr; ホーム](NAVIGATION.md)"

#: results.md:3
msgid "Results"
msgstr "結果"

#: results.md:5
msgid ""
"In our previous paper [[1]](#1), we ran around 300 short trajectories and "
"identified dissociation pathways shown in Figure, where each pathway is "
"named pwa, pwb, ..., and by T4L helices through which benzene dissociated."
msgstr ""
"以前の論文 [[1]](#1) では、約300本の短い Trajectories を実行し、図に示す Dissociation Pathways "
"を特定した。各 Pathway は pwa、pwb、…のほか、Benzene が通過した T4L の Helices で命名している。"

#: results.md:7
msgid ""
"Using the parameters selected in this tutorial, we should be able to obtain "
"one of these pathways within 10 ns."
msgstr "このチュートリアルのパラメータでは、10 ns 以内にこれらの Pathways のいずれかが得られるはずである。"

#: results.md:11
msgid ""
"In the example calculated here, the simulation ends around 2.5 ns, resulting"
" in an unbinding pathway shown below. To find an exit from T4L, the pulling "
"direction of benzene was optimized three times (at 0, 1, and 2 ns)."
msgstr ""
"ここでの例は約2.5 ns で終了し、下に示す Unbinding Pathway が得られる。T4L からの出口を探すため、Benzene の "
"Pulling Direction を0、1、2 ns の3回最適化した。"

#: results.md:13
msgid ""
"By displaying overlayed conformations of the T4L-benzene complex sampled "
"during the simulation, we can see which helices fluctuate the most during "
"the dissociation."
msgstr ""
"Sampling した T4L-Benzene Complex の Conformations を重ねて表示すると、Dissociation 中にどの "
"Helices が最も大きくゆらぐかを確認できる。"

#: results.md:17
msgid ""
"The next figure shows how the loss function behaves in time. We can see that"
" starting from 1.5 ns, it decays to zero, which means that benzene unbinds "
"from the binding pocket of T4L and diffuses toward solvent."
msgstr ""
"次の図は、Loss Function の時間変化を示す。1.5 ns から0へ減衰しており、Benzene が T4L の Binding Pocket"
" から Unbinding し、溶媒へ拡散することを表している。"

#: results.md:21
msgid ""
"This point also coincides with the peak in the bias potential, suggesting "
"that this is the point where benzene overcomes the highest energy barrier."
msgstr ""
"この時点は BiasPotential のピークとも一致しており、Benzene が最も高い Energy Barrier を越える時点と考えられる。"

#: results.md:25
msgid ""
"*Note* Dissociation pathways obtained using the `maze` module can define "
"reference frames for path collective variables, which can be used to run a "
"metadynamics simulation and calculate a free-energy profile. For further "
"details on this, see [here](https://www.plumed.org/doc-v2.9/user-"
"doc/html/_p_a_t_h.html)."
msgstr ""
"*注意* `maze` で得られた Dissociation Pathways は、Path Collective Variables の "
"Reference Frames として使える。その CVs で Metadynamics を行えば、自由エネルギー Profile "
"を計算できる。詳細は[こちら](https://www.plumed.org/doc-v2.9/user-"
"doc/html/_p_a_t_h.html)を参照してほしい。"
